          "message": {
            "text": "CI sample 31469684313 proved AppKit nominated .SFNS-Regular but the resolver still fell through because protected dot-prefixed system faces cannot be reopened with CTFontCreateWithName. Blink retains the AppKit-created handle; Domotion must route that nomination to its path-opened sf-pro key while leaving systemUiPrimary false because the selection came through MatchFontFamily.",
            "markdown": "CI sample 31469684313 proved AppKit nominated .SFNS-Regular but the resolver still fell through because protected dot-prefixed system faces cannot be reopened with CTFontCreateWithName. Blink retains the AppKit-created handle; Domotion must route that nomination to its path-opened sf-pro key while leaving systemUiPrimary false because the selection came through MatchFontFamily."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/render/font-resolution.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 8468,
                  "endLine": 8485,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "      ? resolveFamilyStyleMatch(name, { weight: 400, italic: false, stretch: 100 })\n      : null;\n    // AppKit can hand Blink a protected system-font member that CoreText will\n    // not let another client reopen by its dot-prefixed PostScript name. Blink\n    // keeps that NSFont/CTFont handle; our equivalent is the existing SFNS file\n    // key. Keep `stackPrimaryIsSystemUi` false for this route: it came through\n    // MatchFontFamily, not MatchSystemUIFont, even though both selected SFNS.\n    if (darwinFamilyMatch?.postscriptName.startsWith(\".SFNS-\") === true) {\n      return \"sf-pro\";\n    }\n    const installed = darwinFamilyMatch != null\n      ? resolveInstalledFont(darwinFamilyMatch.postscriptName)\n      : resolveInstalledFont(name);\n    if (installed != null) {\n      const key = `sysfb:${installed.postscriptName}`;\n      // DM-1721: `resolvedAxes` carries DirectWrite's pinned axis values for\n      // variable-face matches (e.g. \"Segoe UI Variable Text\" → opsz 10.5 at\n      // every size) so the hinted-subset pin embeds the instance Chrome paints."
                  }
                }
              }
